<title>UK: British Energy says gets debt ratings.</title>
<headline>British Energy says gets debt ratings.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Energy Plc said on Monday its seven-year, 10-year and 20-year bonds totalling 440 million stg have been assigned long term ratings of A2 by Moody's Investor Services and A minus by Standard and Poor's.  </p>
<p>British Energy also said Moody's have assigned an indicative short-term rating of P1.</p>
<p>British Energy said in a statement the bonds are currently held by HM Treasury.</p>
<p>The company also announced that the general syndication of its 500 million stg banking facility was formalised last week.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 6176</p>
